From 95e599c8f54b66defa47b57b0f3b7e119110e0c7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Esdras Silva <esdrasdev0@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 06:59:41 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] ofh/dpdk: MACsec SecY engine (prototype) in the DPDK Ethernet
 transmitter/receiver

TX: SecTAG inserted during the copy into the mbuf, ICV appended, AES-256-GCM-XPN in a
DPDK cryptodev burst. RX: verified in place after rte_eth_rx_burst, before rte_vlan_strip.
SAs in 4 slots with epoch-based retirement; PN reserved atomically; control socket thread
(INSTALL/ACTIVATE/RETIRE/STATUS). Enabled with OCUDU_MACSEC=1 (environment); disabled
leaves the data path unchanged. Port MTU grows by 32 B and the mbuf pool is sized for it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
